{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Lift up</b> — the meaning is like: <i>Arise, YHWH</i>. Rabbi Moses the Kohen said: כי למשואות is in place of the verb, as if written 'to lift up every evil enemy in the sanctuary' — every enemy who did evil in the sanctuary, for it is inverted like כל תשא עון וקח טוב, the meaning being: every iniquity you bear. And in my opinion: the lamed of למשואות is like the lamed of פן יאמרו לי, lest one say to me, 'behold it is הרימה פעמיך,' on account of your inheritance mentioned above, which is 'the everlasting ruins' — all that the enemy did evil in the sanctuary. And likewise כל תשא עון — every [iniquity] you bear, [then] וקח טוב: take the good that is in our hands, which is the confession of our tongue, for our lips are good at producing, and this vav of וקח טוב, a person cannot understand how it functions, except in the language of Ishmael, where the like of it is a weak pe alef, and thus: טוב ויחיל ודומם, וישא אברהם את עיניו ביום השלישי, ויעזב את עבדיו."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 74, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes several biblical phrases out of order; rendered them exactly as he strings them. The parenthetical 'every [iniquity]' inserts the noun עון only where the syntax becomes wholly opaque in English; kept minimal. The phrase 'our lips are good at producing' renders מפרים uncertainly; the root and intended sense here are textually difficult."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:27.527728461Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}